[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5625643543","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123383#issuecomment-5625643543","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123383","id":5625643543,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT1CCFw","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T21:24:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-11T08:33:31Z","body":"See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121946#issuecomment-5508079234\n\nThe change is intended. Differently specialized container types are ~contra-variant~ invariant.\n\nThere is one special case for untyped containers which we assume could reference any typed container, but that only applies to `Array`/`Array[Variant]`/~`Dictionary`/`Dictionary[Variant, Variant]`~ actually not sure if this was supposed to also be like this for Dictionary, the compiler is deffinetly missing some relevant runtime checks. I can't speak to how robust support for that special case is in the code gen though.