":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5626324027","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123383#issuecomment-5626324027","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123383","id":5626324027,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT1rkOw","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T22:32:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T22:34:13Z","body":"I believe this was closed hastily, or at least not justified clearly enough.\n\n> See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121946#issuecomment-5508079234\n\nYour comment describes a real issue - a function is meant to be accepting `Dictionary[String, int]` but it erroneously accepts the more broad `Dictionary[Variant, int]`. My example is the opposite: a function is meant to return `Dictionary[Variant, String]`, so it should be able to return the more **narrow** `Dictionary[Enum, String]`, but it can't. The justification given here does not address my issue.\n\nAlso this worked in dev4 (and many previous releases) without crashes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5626324027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5626341137","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123383#issuecomment-5626341137","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123383","id":5626341137,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT1snEQ","user":{"login":"sockeye-d","id":106356149,"node_id":"U_kgDOBlbdtQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/106356149?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d","html_url":"https://github.com/sockeye-d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sockeye-d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T22:34:16Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T22:37:59Z","body":"Generally, read/write containers cannot be made co/contravariant in their type parameters, see https://ericlippert.com/2007/10/17/covariance-and-contravariance-in-c-part-2-array-covariance/.\n\ncopied from Discord:\n\nYou can consider a case if the conversion was allowed AND there weren't any runtime type checks,\n```gdscript\nvar a: Dictionary[int, String] = {}\nvar b: Dictionary[Variant, String] = a\nb[\"hello\"] = \"world\"\nprint(a.keys()) # somehow a string got in there??\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5626341137/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5626404087","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123383#issuecomment-5626404087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123383","id":5626404087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABT1wc9w","user":{"login":"MewPurPur","id":85438892,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1NDM4ODky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85438892?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur","html_url":"https://github.com/MewPurPur","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MewPurPur/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-10T22:41:18Z","updated_at":"2026-09-10T22:41:18Z","body":"Oof, yeah that makes sense.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5626404087/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":